    q("A major criticism of military government is that it", ["cannot be removed by the ballot", "makes too many laws", "holds too many elections", "has no army"], 0, "The absence of a peaceful means of removal is the defining weakness of any military government. It is not criticised for holding too many elections."),
    q("Which of the following bodies was used by the military to try civilians?", ["The special military tribunal", "The Supreme Court", "The Federal Civil Service Commission", "The National Assembly"], 0, "The special tribunals were set up outside the ordinary court system, which is why they are treated as an instrument of military rule."),
    q("The 1963 Republican Constitution was suspended by", ["the January 1966 coup", "the 1979 election", "the 1999 transition", "the 1976 local government reform"], 0, "The first coup suspended the Republican Constitution, beginning the military period. The 1979 Constitution ended it, and the 1999 Constitution belongs to the Fourth Republic."),
    q("The main lesson of the military period for Nigerian federalism is that", ["the centre was strengthened at the expense of the states", "the states became stronger than the centre", "the regions were restored", "local government was abolished"], 0, "State creation, the abolition of the regions and the concentration of revenue all strengthened the centre, which is the federalism point the paper draws from Chapter 5."),
